Brave: send safesearch/country/ui_lang as URL parameters instead of
cookies. search.brave.com answers 429 to any request with a cookie
(even one alone) from som's egress (2026-11), and 200 to the same request
without; it honours the URL parameters the same way. No upstream issue
yet; upstream's engine still sets the cookies (master a7128d5d).

Scope: brave.py's request() serves every Brave engine of settings.yml
(brave, brave.images, brave.videos, brave.news, brave.goggles), so all of
them go cookie-less. Dropped without a replacement: the `useLocation=0`
and `summarizer=0` cookies. Brave then may localise by the egress IP
(the `country` parameter still names the region) and may add its
summarizer block, which the result parser ignores.

